  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vanuatu Earthquake Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 17 December 2024, Vanuatu was struck by a 7.3 magnitude earthquake which impacted an estimated 80,000 people and caused significant damage to Vanuatu&#x2019;s capital Port Vila. This investment is Australia&apos;s immediate response to the earthquake and includes support for the Vanuatu Government&apos;s response efforts, including support for vulnerable groups including women, children and people with disability. Activities include the deployment of emergency medical and disaster response teams, provision of relief supplies, and funding for humanitarian partners including UNICEF, the Australian Red Cross and Australian Humanitarian Partnership NGOs operating in Vanuatu.</narrative>
  </description>
